Gives WebGPU layer groups the context's observer, so a drawable that throws is
reported instead of crashing the renderer. The OpenGL, Metal, and Vulkan
contexts call setObserver() on each layer group they create, but the WebGPU
context didn't, and LayerGroupBase left the pointer uninitialized. When a
drawable's upload threw, for example std::bad_alloc on a full wasm heap,
visitDrawables() called onRenderError() through that pointer. A browser module
then trapped with "memory access out of bounds" and left a black canvas. The
WebGPU context now sets the observer, and the pointer starts at the null
observer, as gfx::Context's does, for a layer group that is never given one.
Upstream: https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native/pull/4922

diff --git a/include/mln/renderer/layer_group.hpp b/include/mln/renderer/layer_group.hpp
index ee3e5a8..d0db7f0 100644
--- a/include/mln/renderer/layer_group.hpp
+++ b/include/mln/renderer/layer_group.hpp
@@ -117,7 +117,7 @@ protected:
     int32_t layerIndex;
     std::vector<LayerTweakerWeakPtr> layerTweakers;
     std::string name;
-    gfx::ContextObserver* observer;
+    gfx::ContextObserver* observer = &gfx::Context::nullObserver;
 };
 
 /**
diff --git a/src/mln/webgpu/context.cpp b/src/mln/webgpu/context.cpp
index b534ded..7e0c8c8 100644
--- a/src/mln/webgpu/context.cpp
+++ b/src/mln/webgpu/context.cpp
@@ -118,11 +118,13 @@ gfx::ShaderProgramBasePtr Context::getGenericShader(gfx::ShaderRegistry& registr
 
 TileLayerGroupPtr Context::createTileLayerGroup(int32_t layerIndex, std::size_t initialCapacity, std::string name) {
     auto tileLayerGroup = std::make_shared<webgpu::TileLayerGroup>(layerIndex, initialCapacity, std::move(name));
+    tileLayerGroup->setObserver(observer);
     return tileLayerGroup;
 }
 
 LayerGroupPtr Context::createLayerGroup(int32_t layerIndex, std::size_t initialCapacity, std::string name) {
     auto layerGroup = std::make_shared<webgpu::LayerGroup>(layerIndex, initialCapacity, std::move(name));
+    layerGroup->setObserver(observer);
     return layerGroup;
 }
 
